      "role": "user",
      "content": "A 2% increase? That's interesting. \n\nTo be honest, I'm looking at the actual comment threads from the primary demographic right now, and it looks pretty messy. I'm seeing a lot of heated reactions and people expressing real frustration with the stance the candidate took. \n\nCan you walk me through the specific data points that show an increase? I want to make sure I understand how the sentiment is tilting positive if the visible engagement looks so reactive. Are there specific sub-groups or platforms where this positive spike is coming from?",
